{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And you shall be to Me a kingdom of priests.</b> And through this you will be a treasure above all others, for you will be a kingdom of priests to comprehend and to instruct the entire human species, so as to call all of them in the name of YHWH and to serve Him with a single resolve — as the matter of Israel will be in the time to come, as it says: וְאַתֶּם כֹּהֲנֵי ה' תִּקָּרֵאוּ (Isaiah 61:6), and as it says: כִּי מִצִּיּוֹן תֵּצֵא תוֹרָה (Isaiah 2:3)." "<b>And a holy nation.</b> Not subject to corruption, but enduring forever in each individual — as the matter will be in the time to come, as it says: וְהָיָה הַנִּשְׁאָר בְּצִיּוֹן וְהַנּוֹתָר בִּירוּשָׁלַיִם קָדוֹשׁ יֵאָמֶר לוֹ (Isaiah 4:3). And the Sages of blessed memory said (Sanhedrin 92a): just as the Holy One is eternal, so are they eternal. And this is because indeed the intent of the blessed El in giving the Torah was to bestow upon them then all the destined good, had they not corrupted their way with the calf, as it says: וַיִּתְנַצְּלוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת עֶדְיָם מֵהַר חוֹרֵב (Exodus 33:6)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:18.245863235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}